      <div class="intro-text" id="food-intro">
        <p>Start with a plate of Antalya’s own <strong>piyaz</strong> — white beans with tahini — then work your way through grilled fish, meze and slow evenings by the harbour. Kaleiçi has courtyard restaurants inside Ottoman houses; Lara and Konyaaltı do seafood with sea views; Kaş and Kalkan are made for long dinners on rooftop terraces.</p>
        <p>A clear word on Michelin: the <a href="https://www.michelin.com/en/publications/products-and-services/the-michelin-guide-turkiye-reveals-its-2026-restaurant-selection">MICHELIN Guide Türkiye 2026</a> does not cover Antalya, so we don’t label any restaurant here as starred or selected.</p>
        <p>Menus, opening hours and reservation policies change. Each profile links to the restaurant’s own page — confirm before you go.</p>
